All done. Here's what I added:

**`txtar/archive.go`** — `Lookup` method (inserted before `Format`, matching the neighbouring style):
```go
// Lookup returns the file with the given name, or nil and false
// when the archive has no such file.
func (a *Archive) Lookup(name string) (*File, bool) {
	for i, f := range a.Files {
		if f.Name == name {
			return &a.Files[i], true
		}
	}
	return nil, false
}
```
Note: I used `&a.Files[i]` (index-based loop) rather than `&f` (range variable) so the returned pointer points into the archive's actual slice — callers can mutate the file data and it reflects in `a.Files`.

**`txtar/archive_test.go`** — `TestLookup` covering both outcomes:
- Found file (`"foo"` and `"bar"`) — checks `ok == true` and correct `Name`/`Data`.
- Not-found file (`"baz"`) — checks `ok == false` and `f == nil`.

**Tests pass:** `go test ./txtar/` → `ok`

